[
    {
        "id": "g100-example-tab",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "G100 Compliance",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "# G100/2 Compliance with Victron\n\nThis flow monitors grid import/export against the agreed MEL/MIL limits and enforces Stage 2/3 lockout per the ENA EREC G100 Issue 2 specification.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. **Grid Power**: Read from Victron grid meter (negative = export, positive = import)\n2. **AC Source**: Tells the node when the grid is the active AC source. Enforcement is suspended on generator or shore power.\n3. **Lockout output**: Fires only when lockout state changes. Wire this to your relay or ESS control to stop exporting when `true`.\n4. **Status output**: Full G100 state on every reading — stage, excursion counts, reset eligibility.\n\n## Setup\n\nUpdate the Victron service IDs to match your installation:\n- Grid meter: `com.victronenergy.grid/XX`\n- System:     `com.victronenergy.system/0`\n- VE.Bus:     `com.victronenergy.vebus/XXX`\n\nConfigure the g100 node with your agreed MEL (export limit, negative W) and optionally MIL (import limit, positive W).\n\n## Reset\n\nFor domestic installations, send `{ topic: 'reset' }` to reset from Stage 3. For commercial, include the installer password: `{ topic: 'reset', payload: { password: 1234 } }`."
    },
    {
